First and foremost, we extend our heartfelt thanks to our academic supervisor, Dr. Mai El Defrawi, whose expert guidance, invaluable feedback, and constant encouragement throughout every phase of this project have been indispensable. Her professional insights and unwavering dedication to academic excellence have shaped this work tremendously.

We are also deeply grateful to the Faculty of Computers and Information at our university, and to the Department of Information Systems, for providing us with the academic foundation, resources, and environment necessary to undertake a project of this scope and complexity.

Our sincere thanks go to our families for their endless patience, moral support, and encouragement during the long and demanding hours of development and research. Their belief in our capabilities sustained us throughout this journey.

We also acknowledge the open-source communities behind .NET 8, ASP.NET Core, React.js, FastAPI, and the Google Gemini AI API, whose tools and libraries made this project technically feasible.

Finally, we dedicate this work to every elderly individual who deserves dignity, professional care, and compassionate monitoring in their golden years. It is our hope that the SmartElderlyCare system will, in some measure, contribute to improving the quality of eldercare in our society.

Team Members:
Anton Farid Maurice, Haidy Medhat Azer, Maryam Elghazaly Abdelkader,
Mahmoud Mohammed Mahmoud Elbarbary, Abdallah Essam Mohammed, Abdelrhman Reda Sayed""", size=11)

    add_page_break(doc)

    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    # ABSTRACT
    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    add_heading(doc, "Abstract", 1)

    add_paragraph(doc, """SmartElderlyCare (commercially branded as SilverNest) is a comprehensive, multi-tier elder care management platform developed as a graduation project for the Faculty of Computers and Information, Information Systems Department. The system addresses critical challenges in managing elderly residents at care facilities by integrating modern software engineering technologies into a unified, intelligent solution.

The system is built using a clean three-tier microservices architecture comprising: (1) a .NET 8 / ASP.NET Core Web API backend implementing Clean Architecture (Domain, Application, Infrastructure, and API layers) with Entity Framework Core and SQL Server; (2) a Python FastAPI AI microservice incorporating a trained Random Forest machine learning model for health risk prediction, a meal recommendation engine, and a fall detection prototype; and (3) a React.js 19 single-page application frontend integrated with the Google Gemini AI API for intelligent, natural-language daily report generation.

The platform serves four distinct user roles: System Administrators, Team Leaders, Care Employees, and Family Members. Key functional modules include: automated JWT-based authentication with role-based access control (RBAC), real-time SignalR-based push notifications, daily health metric reporting with AI-generated summaries, predictive health risk analytics with clinical rule-based overrides, AI-powered personalised dietary recommendations, family visit scheduling and management, employee work schedule management, attendance tracking with clock-in/clock-out, approval workflows, comprehensive audit logging, and a full administrative dashboard with system-wide statistics.

The AI microservice was trained on a custom elderly health dataset of over 500 records spanning vital signs, medication adherence, mobility, sleep patterns, and dietary intake. The trained Random Forest classifier achieves high accuracy in predicting high-risk health events, supplemented by a hybrid clinical rule engine that enforces hard clinical thresholds for patient safety.

The project demonstrates the successful application of full-stack software engineering principles, machine learning, natural language processing, real-time communication, and human-computer interaction design to a meaningful real-world healthcare problem.

Keywords: Elder Care Management, ASP.NET Core, React.js, Python FastAPI, Machine Learning, Random Forest, Health Risk Prediction, Gemini AI, SignalR, Clean Architecture, JWT Authentication, RBAC, Information Systems.""", size=11)

